{% twoColumns reverseOnMobile=true %}
## Connor Miller - Site Director

Connor Miller is an operations leader and entrepreneur who combines a background in business management with a deep passion for youth and young adult discipleship. He graduated from Bethel University in 2016 with a B.A. in Business Administration and minor in Marketing. During high school and college years, he co-founded two small businesses.&nbsp;

Eventually, Connor discovered a genuine love for camping ministry while serving as a camp counselor for two summers. In 2018 he sold his business assets and joined full time at Bear Lake Camp in Albion, Indiana, as Business Manager, a role he held through 2025. In 2020, he also stepped into the role of Director of Operations at Camp Otyokwah, where he helped oversee the logistics, systems, and day-to-day operations of both ministries. In 2026 he became the Site Director at Otyokwah.

Driven by a desire to see young adults become more like Christ, Connor seeks to bring together practical leadership and intentional discipleship. His goal is to help cultivate environments where young people can discover that their identity is primarily in Christ, develop healthy boundaries, make wise decisions, and learn what it looks like to live out their faith in everyday life.

